## Verdict
First give a brief reasoning (a few sentences — this is a shallow sanity check, not a deep review). Then, on the FINAL line, state the verdict as:

  Verdict: <VERDICT>

where <VERDICT> is exactly one of:
- PASS — substantive, on-topic content is present. It need not be complete, deep, perfectly formatted, or wrapped in any tags; PASS as long as the main work is genuinely there.
- UPDATE: <what to fix> — real, on-topic work is present but it is incomplete (missing large parts of what was asked) or has a format problem. We preserve it and revise/complete it in place; state concretely what to fix right after the "UPDATE:".
- RETRY: <why> — the output is fundamentally unusable: empty, wildly off-topic, or narration-only (it only describes what it would do but never does it). A fresh attempt from scratch is needed.

The final line MUST begin with "Verdict:" immediately followed by PASS, UPDATE, or RETRY — no quotes, no code fence, and nothing after it. Put any reason on that same line, right after the verdict keyword.
